SUMMARY:Sam Kissajukian: 300 Paintings
DESCRIPTION:Run Time: 80 minutes\, no intermission  \n\n\nIn 2021\, Sydney comedian Sam Kissajukian decided to quit standup\, rent an abandoned cake factory\, and become a painter. Over the course of a six-month manic episode\, he created 300 large-scale paintings\, unknowingly documenting his mental state through the process. In this hilarious\, fascinating\, and wildly original show\, Kissajukian brings audiences on a rollercoaster ride that explores the ties between art\, mental health\, and creativity. Each performance includes post-show access to an art exhibit featuring Kissajukian and his works.    \n\n\n“Beautifully frank.” (The New Yorker)  \n\n\n“A whimsical delight!” (The New York Times)
URL:https://www.peakperfs.org/event/sam-kissajukian-300-paintings/
CATEGORIES:2026 - 2027
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.peakperfs.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/300-paintings.jpg
END:VEVENT
